One parity table per logical stack, and two sequence fixes it exposed

Sequence-aligning our AP->CP stream against stock's on identical firmware, per
stack, up to each stack's first IMS context:

    ch 0xf5 Telus   130/196 in order    66%   (was 59% before the preamble)
    ch 0xf6 Fizz     70/198 in order    35%   (was 31%)

ch 0xf6 stays far behind because the table could not represent it. It is
generated from one channel, and the two differ in substance: ch 0xf6 sends
0x0605 and 0x0c14, which 0xf5 never sends at all, and its pre-context block is
sixteen requests where 0xf5's is seven -- 0x0d3a, 0x0d3c and 0x0d17 appear only
there. Replaying 0xf5's boot on 0xf6 cannot fix that by substitution.

So generate one table per stack from the same capture. This also retires
`primary_only`: a request stock makes once for the whole AP simply appears in
stack 0's table and not in stack 1's, which is what the flag was emulating. The
generator confirms the equivalence -- ids unique to stack 0 come out as exactly
0x0404, 0x090b and 0x1307, the three the flag had marked.

    stack 0 (ch 0xf5)  120 rows, 39 ids, PRE_PDN 7
    stack 1 (ch 0xf6)  118 rows, 38 ids, PRE_PDN 16
    ids only in stack 0: 0x0404, 0x090b, 0x1307
    ids only in stack 1: 0x0605, 0x0c14

Two further divergences the alignment showed, both now fixed:

**The attach re-assert goes back to the unscoped form.** It had been narrowed to
the attach APN's own context on the theory that re-asserting ahead of a foreign
APN cost a grant. That was a false attribution. Measured across three boots, an
attach went out just before ch 0xf6's first attempt every time -- r36 granted,
r38 refused, r42 refused -- so it does not discriminate. Stock does not scope it
either: its ch 0xf5 re-assert is followed 1306 ms later by a context for `ims`.
Narrowing it only lost the parity, because ch 0xf5 never asks for a context on
its own attach APN at all, so the scoped form never fired on the stack that
needs it.

**The profile set is pushed twice, back to back.** Stock pushes its whole set at
9930 ms, again at 10709 ms and a third time at 10720 ms, 11 ms apart and 518 ms
before its context. We pushed it once, then the single profile
mm_sit_client_setup_data_call() registers for the APN it is about to ask for --
so the last profile frame the CP saw was a lone `ims` where stock's was the
complete table.

What this does NOT address, named here so it is not mistaken for an oversight:
stock requests the data context before the IMS context on a stack that has
mobile data (ch 0xf6: data cid 17 at 10387 ms, ims cid 18 at 11332 ms), and we
ask for IMS first with an empty PDN list, which is refused -- our attempt 2,
after data is up, is granted. That ordering is not the plugin's to choose: the
data context is requested by NetworkManager. Gating IMS on it would stall every
stack that never gets mobile data, which is exactly the Telus stack, so the
retry ladder stays the mechanism. It also does not explain Telus, whose own
stock capture shows an empty PDN list at the moment it asks and a grant anyway.

